[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Worst-case audit evidence and refinement admission

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-WORST-EVIDENCE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Preserve the worst normalized evidence including unavailable failure metrics
STATEMENT: >>>
Audit merging shall retain the greatest absolute discrepancy divided by its
effective tolerance per identifier. A failed check missing either discrepancy
or tolerance shall outrank finite measured evidence. Distinct identifiers shall
remain distinct. An equal severity shall retain the first evidence, including
its discrepancy, tolerance and explanatory sample context.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The deterministic first-on-tie rule records existing behavior as a draft
requirement; it is not a new physics or global-accuracy guarantee.
Verification: tests/audit_refinement_contracts.rs a_failed_check_missing_either_metric_outranks_finite_evidence,
normalized_severity_matches_exact_rational_cross_products (128 cases, seed2026111907),
equal_normalized_severity_retains_the_first_evidence_and_distinct_ids.
The randomized oracle uses bounded exact integer cross products, not the
floating-point division used by implementation. Implementation: AuditReport::merge_worst.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-REFINEMENT-ADMISSION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Validate refinement dimensions and selected axes independently
STATEMENT: >>>
Refinement comparison shall reject each nonfinite or nonpositive absolute or
relative bound, unsupported unit, empty coarse input, non-finer fine input,
negative or nonfinite sample time, non-increasing axis and unavailable/nonfinite
selected signal. A malformed input shall return a typed error rather than a
passing report or panic. Independent invalid inputs shall not require another
invalid field to activate admission checks.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: refinement_bounds_units_and_empty_input_are_independent_admission_checks
and malformed_shared_axes_and_selected_signals_are_refused. Matching negative
or positive-infinite axis points in both runs prevent incidental later
no-match failures from hiding deficient admission. Implementation: compare_refinement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: AUDIT-REFINEMENT-SHARED-POINTS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Report observed normalized change at exactly shared points
STATEMENT: >>>
Refinement shall compare selected signals only at exactly shared coarse sample
times and report the worst normalized difference with its physical bound,
unit and sample context. Unmatched fine midpoints shall not be interpolated
into that comparison. The result shall explicitly distinguish observed change
from a global numerical error bound.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: refinement_selects_normalized_shared_point_change_without_global_accuracy_claims.
The analytical fixture has ratios 1/0.2=5 and 2/1.1<2; an unmatched midpoint
has value99. V and A units retain the same known selected-point calculation.
<<<
